    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Foster is a rural town located in southwestern Garvin County, Oklahoma.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        14,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foster%2C_Oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office was established in Foster on August 12, 1891, and may have been named for the first postmaster, Noah Foster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=FO059"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town of Foster was surveyed and platted in October 1902, with the plat approved by the Department of the Interior in 1903.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=FO059"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Foster became an official part of Garvin County when Oklahoma achieved statehood in 1907.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=FO059"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A Masonic lodge was organized in Foster around 1902, and a public school was established by 1907.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.okhistory.org/publications/enc/entry?entry=FO059"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "By 1910, Foster supported a variety of businesses, including a hotel, a drug store, and Mullens's cotton gin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        28,
        29
      ],
